 ## Model and cost rules
 
 - Tiers resolve in `llm.default_model()` from `CF_MODEL` / `CF_CHEAP_MODEL` / `CF_STRONG_MODEL`, else the `LLM_PROVIDER` default. `CF_MODEL` (main: drilling, explaining, reconcile-by-default) defaults to `claude-sonnet-5-5` (`claude-sonnet-5` on kernal, `gpt-6-luna` on gateway). `CF_CHEAP_MODEL` (cards, notes, quiz distractors, garble cleaning) defaults to `claude-haiku-4-5` (anthropic), `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (openrouter), `gemini-2.5-flash` (kernal), `gpt-6-luna` (gateway). `CF_STRONG_MODEL` (reconcile only) defaults to the main tier. The `.env*.example` files show older sample values; code defaults win.
-- The **gateway lane** (`gateway.py`) runs only the allow-listed bulk jobs (`cards`, `concepts`, `syllabus`, `oral`) on `CF_GATEWAY_MODEL` at `CF_GATEWAY_BASE` (code default `gpt-6-luna` on the LiteLLM gateway; production points it at a dead OpenRouter free model, and `CF_GATEWAY=off` is pending in `docs/pending-protected/cf-gateway-off.patch`), and falls back to `CF_CHEAP_MODEL`. The tutor never uses it. Production runs `LLM_PROVIDER=kernal`: main tier `claude-sonnet-5` (Anthropic API), cheap tier `gemini-2.5-flash` (Vertex AI, us-central1), both via the Kernal router. Read `docs/privacy-gateway.md` (the GDPR record) before widening it.
